{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"a8e50a7d-6fd1-4ae1-b05b-14691b98db00","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Slope-intercept form describes a straight line using its starting height and its slope.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"form","region":"A1","latex":"y=mx+b"},{"op":"axes","id":"lineaxes","region":"right","x":{"min":-1,"max":4,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":-1,"max":9,"label":"y"}},{"op":"text","id":"roles","anchor":{"el":"form","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"m: slope     b: y-intercept"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"a8e50a7d-6fd1-4ae1-b05b-14691b98db00","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"a8e50a7d-6fd1-4ae1-b05b-14691b98db00","step":{"id":"s2","script":"For y equals two x plus one, the y-intercept is one. Start at zero, one on the vertical axis.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"roles","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"y=2x+1"},{"op":"curve","id":"straight","axes_id":"lineaxes","expr":"2*x+1","domain":[-1,4]},{"op":"text","id":"intercept","anchor":{"el":"example","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"y-intercept: (0, 1)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"a8e50a7d-6fd1-4ae1-b05b-14691b98db00","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"a8e50a7d-6fd1-4ae1-b05b-14691b98db00","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The slope is two: move right one and rise two. That takes us from zero, one to one, three.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"run","axes_id":"lineaxes","expr":"1","domain":[0,1]},{"op":"equation","id":"movement","anchor":{"el":"example","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"(0,1)\\to(1,1)\\to(1,3)\\quad\\text{right }1,\\ \\text{up }2"},{"op":"equation","id":"slope","anchor":{"el":"movement","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"m=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}=\\frac{2}{1}=2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Starting at (1, 3), what point comes next if you move right one and rise two?","expected_gist":"(2, 5)"}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"a8e50a7d-6fd1-4ae1-b05b-14691b98db00","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Repeat the same move to reach two, five. Every point on this line follows y equals two x plus one.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"thirdpoint","construct":{"kind":"along","element_id":"straight","t":0.6},"label":"(2, 5)"},{"op":"equation","id":"check","anchor":{"el":"slope","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"x=2\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad y=2(2)+1=5"}],"checkpoint":null}}
